Package: n5max-sata-lpm-fix
Source: n5max-sata-lpm-fix
Version: 1.0.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Alpha Area <awpak78@hotmail.com>
Installed-Size: 8
Depends: udev, systemd
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/minisforum-docs/N5-MAX-Docs
Description: Keep N5 MAX SATA link power management at max_performance
 The N5 MAX SATA controller (a JMicron JMB585 driving the five HDD bays)
 fails to wake reliably from the 'Partial' SATA link power state that the
 min_power_with_partial policy enables by default on some kernels. The
 resulting link resets can cause I/O errors and filesystem corruption.
 .
 This package installs a udev rule and a systemd oneshot service that set
 link_power_management_policy to max_performance for all SCSI hosts, at
 installation time and on every boot.
